module bindings.go.pprof_cmdline_handler_exposure;

// net/http/pprof documents Cmdline as the handler that "responds with the
// running program's command line, with arguments separated by NUL bytes",
// and documents the package as a set of handlers to be registered on a
// mux, serving them under /debug/pprof/ by default. Four of the five
// handlers in that set -- Index, Profile, Symbol, Trace -- report runtime
// profiling state; Cmdline alone answers with the process's own
// arguments. A server that takes its configuration as flags -- a shared
// key, a datastore URI with inline credentials, a TLS key path -- carries
// all of it in argv, so wiring pprof.Cmdline onto a served mux publishes
// the operator's arguments to whoever can reach that port. The debug
// exposure concept covers it: the command line is the program's
// configuration, serialized into an HTTP response (CWE-215).
//
// The Go frontend records each call argument's selector path as a call_arg
// token on the registering function's context, so the handler value handed
// to a router's registration method is visible here. The predicate is
// AST-routed and function-confined in Go, so a selector reference anywhere
// in the same function satisfies it, which also covers a handler held in a
// local variable before registration -- the route stays inside the
// function that wires the handler. The other four pprof handlers are
// deliberately not matched: none of them answers with the process's
// arguments, and serving them behind the same mux is a documented,
// supported configuration.
//
// Two recall residuals, stated rather than hidden. An import of the
// package under another name spells the selector differently and is not
// matched, and the blank side-effect import registers the default-mux
// routes without referencing Cmdline at all, so neither form is covered.
binding goPprofCmdlineHandlerExposure {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function"
    and node.context.language == "go"
    and node.context.callArg contains "pprof.Cmdline"
  emit issue code.DebugInfoExposure at node
}
